# oracle: LJ fluid whose atom types and x velocities are set every 10 steps by fix set (type v_t2 vx v_t, per-atom variables that do not depend on positions), reneighbor yes, neighbor lists rebuilt every step (see the report: a mid-run type change needs it in the engine)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.3e-14, atoms 1.1e-13.
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
mass            2 1.2
velocity        all create 1.0 87287 loop all
variable        t atom 0.5*sin(step*0.1)+0.01*id
variable        t2 atom 1+(id>54)
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
pair_coeff      1 2 1.0 1.05 2.5
pair_coeff      2 2 0.9 1.1 2.5
timestep        0.002
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check no
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all set 10 1 atom 1*108 type v_t2 vx v_t
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             100
